# --- Note ---
# data/, img/, rdf/ and docs/ are part of the reproducible archive.

# --- Generated SQL drop-ins ---
# The PostgreSQL statements are NOT in this repository. They name the tables,
# columns and quality flags of a live database that also answers a public web
# application, and nothing here needs them: the pipeline reads REST. What is
# tracked instead is sql/MANIFEST.json — sizes, hashes and the revision — so
# that two people can tell whether they hold the same statement without the
# statement being published. See py/sql_manifest.py.
#
# Removing them from a clone is not enough on its own: they were tracked
# until now, so they remain in the history. See sql/README.md.
sql/*.sql

# sql/IPSDatedSites.sql WAS the goldstandard and was tracked: it is what gets
# cited, diffed and blamed. What lands here is derived from it by
# py/make_sql.py — the ColdFusion drop-in and the psql form. Committing them
# would create a second copy of the model that can drift without anyone
# noticing which one produced a given export.
sql/generated/

# --- This repository ---
# rdf/, img/ and docs/ are generated but ARE part of the archive:
# they are the deliverable and must be diffable. Do not ignore them.
# The SVGs are byte-stable (SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH + fixed svg.hashsalt), so a
# rebuild without a content change leaves git status clean.

README-PATCH.md

# --- The build report ---
# docs/run-report.* is a record of ONE run on ONE machine, not a derived
# artefact of the data. It contains the file inventory of the working tree,
# the tools that happened to be installed (GraphViz present or absent
# changes the log itself) and the platform's path separators. It therefore
# cannot be byte-identical between a Windows checkout and a Linux runner,
# and demanding that it be is a category error: the report's whole purpose
# is to say what happened here, this time.
#
# Everything else in docs/ is generated from the code and the data alone
# and is deterministic on any platform, which is what makes the staleness
# check in CI meaningful. Keeping the report out preserves that.
#
# To publish one deliberately — for a release, say — write it elsewhere:
#   python py/main.py --report-out docs/releases/2026-08
docs/run-report.html
docs/run-report.txt
